DRM audio patch for Dream 2.2 (dream_2.2.orig.tar.gz, SourceForge project drm).
Apply with:  patch -p1 -d <dream-2.2 source root> < dream22_drm_audio.patch
Produced 2026-07-29 for the radiotuna DRM campaign (task #34).

These are modifications to Dream, which is GPL-2.0-or-later, copyright
Volker Fischer, Alexander Kurpiers, Julian Cable, David Flamand et al.,
TU Darmstadt / BBC / Fraunhofer IIS.  This patch is therefore also
GPL-2.0-or-later.  Original source: https://sourceforge.net/projects/drm

What it changes, and why (full write-up in drm_day_log.md):
  * sourcedecoders/AudioCodec.cpp    - try faad2 before fdk-aac for legacy
      DRM AAC.  Mainline fdk-aac parses the DRM SDC config but cannot decode
      DRM30 ER-AAC-SCAL, so it claimed the service and then failed every
      frame.  fdk-aac stays as the AAC fallback and the only xHE-AAC decoder.
  * sourcedecoders/aac_codec.cpp     - AacCodec::Decode() never returned a
      value, so every successfully decoded faad2 frame was discarded.
      Also bound the sample copy to the caller-s buffer.
  * MSC/xheaacsuperframe.cpp         - frameBorderCount==0 indexed an empty
      vector (segfault on xHE services); the frame border index is already
      relative to the payload section so the extra -2 corrupted every frame
      (A/B: 673 parse errors with it, 0 without); mono/stereo test compared
      against the enum constant instead of the value.  Follows the -14-line
      fix for xHE-AAC decoding- thread on the Dream forum.
  * sourcedecoders/AudioSourceDecoder.cpp - bigger resampler buffer and a
      divide-by-zero guard for xHE-AAC.
  * sourcedecoders/fdk_aac_codec.cpp - offer fdk a real output buffer on the
      first frame (frameSize/numChannels are only valid after the first
      decode); re-read stream info afterwards; extra config diagnostics.
  * SDC/SDCReceive.cpp               - print the SDC station label, which the
      console build otherwise has no way to show.
  * sound/drm_portaudio.h            - CPaCommon::Enumerate called with 2 of
      its 3 arguments; Dream 2.2 does not compile against portaudio without
      this.

NOTE: fdk-aac must be built from upstream source.  Ubuntu-s packaged
libfdk-aac2 2.0.2-3 segfaults inside aacDecoder_ConfigRaw() on DRM xHE-AAC
configs.  fdk-aac is under the Fraunhofer FDK AAC licence and grants NO
patent licence.

